      "name": "FindAsyncDataNode",
      "signature": "uint FindAsyncDataNode(uint dwId1, uint dwId2, uint dwId3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Search async data list for matching node and validate its state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get head of g_pAsyncDataList global\n2. If list empty, return 0 (not found)\n3. Loop through linked list entries\n4. Get node pointer from list entry at offset 0x0\n5. Check if node valid (not NULL) and bit 0 at offset 0x20 is CLEAR\n6. Compare dwId1 against node[0x0], dwId2 against node[0x4], dwId3 against node[0x8]\n7. If all three IDs match, check field at offset 0xb0 (handle/resource)\n8. If handle is NULL, assert fail with error code 0xa5f\n9. Call Ordinal_10092 to validate/process node\n10. Return 1 if validation succeeds (non-zero result)\n11. Advance to next list entry via pList[5] and loop until NULL\n\nParameters:\n- dwId1 (uint): First identifier to match against node offset 0x0\n- dwId2 (uint): Second identifier to match against node offset 0x4\n- dwId3 (uint): Third identifier to match against node offset 0x8\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Matching node found and validation succeeded\n- 0: No matching node found or validation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Node found but handle field (offset 0xb0) is NULL triggers assertion failure\n- Bit 0 at offset 0x20 must be CLEAR for node to be considered valid\n- Function does NOT return on assertion failure (calls non-returning TerminateProcessWithCode)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
