      "name": "BlitScaledCmpFrameClipped",
      "signature": "void BlitScaledCmpFrameClipped(int * pCmpFile, int nXOffset, int nYOffset, int nDestX, int nDestY, byte * pDestSurface, int nMaxY, uint dwPitch, int nPaletteIndex, byte bTransparency)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Blit scaled CMP frame with vertical clipping to destination surface.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate CMP file pointer and CEL data exists (pCmpFile[1])\n2. Verify CEL version is 6 (standard D2 CMP format)\n3. Verify CEL flags do not have 0x4 set (unsupported compression)\n4. Validate destination surface is non-NULL\n5. Retrieve CMP dimensions from header (width at +0x4, height at +0x8)\n6. Calculate nHalfWidth = frame_offset_y / 2 (center baseline)\n7. Calculate nScaledY = nYOffset + nHalfWidth\n8. Calculate nRowsToDraw = frame_height / 2 (scaled height)\n9. If nScaledY < nRowsToDraw, clamp: nRowsToDraw = nScaledY + 1\n10. Skip if nRowsToDraw <= 0 (entirely above viewport)\n11. If nScaledY > nMaxY, apply bottom clipping and adjust row count\n12. Call DecompressCelData with clipped parameters\n\nParameters:\n- pCmpFile (int*): CMP file structure [0]=pCelData, [1]=pCelHeader\n- nXOffset (int): Source X offset into frame\n- nYOffset (int): Source Y offset into frame\n- nDestX (int): Destination X coordinate\n- nDestY (int): Destination Y coordinate\n- pDestSurface (byte*): Destination surface buffer\n- nMaxY (int): Maximum Y coordinate (clipping boundary)\n- dwPitch (uint): Surface pitch in bytes per scanline\n- nPaletteIndex (int): Palette offset for color remapping\n- bTransparency (byte): Transparency/blitting mode flags\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies destination surface in-place)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6: Expected CEL version for CMP compatibility\n- 0x4: CEL flag mask for unsupported compression\n- 0x4f6, 0x4f7, 0x4fa, 0x4fd: Source line numbers for assertions",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:449e68050137ffb3d02781b1c2e44b59",
