      "name": "DecompressSpriteFrameRLEToBuffer",
      "signature": "void DecompressSpriteFrameRLEToBuffer(dword * pBitmapHeader, dword * pBitStream, dword * pPaletteInfo, dword * pBitStreamControl, byte * pbPaletteData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Decompress RLE-encoded sprite frame data to destination buffer using bit stream input.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate bit stream and palette state (check buffer capacity)\n2. Read 1 control bit from bit stream:\n   - Bit 0: Literal fill - detect palette entry size (1, 2, or 4 bytes)\n   - Bit 1: Copy from palette - read required bits and map through palette table\n3. If literal fill (control bit = 0):\n   - Determine palette entry width (1, 2, or 4 bytes)\n   - Fill entire frame with single palette entry value (replicate byte)\n4. If copy from palette (control bit = 1):\n   - Check if palette matches current palette entry set\n   - If mismatch: clear destination buffer (fill with 0x00)\n   - If match: copy reference palette row to temporary buffer\n   - For each scan line in bitmap:\n     - For each pixel in scan line:\n       - Read N-bit value from bit stream (N = palette entry width in bits)\n       - Index into palette table\n       - Write pixel to destination buffer\n5. Increment palette table pointer by 4 bytes\n6. Return\n\nParameters:\n- pBitmapHeader (IMPLICIT ECX): Pointer to bitmap header structure\n  [0] = bitmap width in pixels\n  [1] = pointer to destination pixel buffer  \n  [2] = scan line stride (bytes per row)\n  [3] = bitmap height in rows\n  [4] = reserved\n- pBitStream (IMPLICIT EDX): Pointer to bit stream control structure\n  [0] = bit stream data buffer base\n  [1] = current read position (pointer to next dword)\n  [2] = buffer capacity (bytes)\n  [3] = current bit offset in dword (0-31)\n  [4] = reserved\n- pPaletteInfo: Pointer to palette info structure\n  [0] = palette entry count\n  [1] = palette pixel buffer pointer\n  [2] = palette scan line stride\n  [3] = palette entry width identifier (1/2/4)\n  [4] = reserved\n- pBitStreamControl: Pointer to bit stream state (same layout as pBitStream)\n- pbPaletteData: Pointer to palette color table (array of palette entries)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n- Modifies destination buffer in place\n- Updates pBitStreamControl pointer (advances by 4 bytes)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Literal fill creates solid color frame (0x01000101 pattern for byte replication)\n- Copy from palette clears buffer first if palette set differs\n- Bit stream must have sufficient capacity or assertion failure triggers\n- Palette entry width determines how many bits read per pixel\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20: 32-bit read granule (32 bits per dword)\n- 0x1F: Bit mask for 32-bit rotation (31 = 32-1)\n- 0x03: Mask for low 2 bits (pixel count modulo 4)\n- 0x4: Palette pointer increment (4 bytes per entry)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:f37eae4b9486cb4175333f44901ab791",
