      "name": "AllocateTileProjectBuffer",
      "signature": "uint AllocateTileProjectBuffer(TileProject * pTileProject)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a TileProject data buffer with zero-filled memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pAllocHeader at +0x5c already allocated - if so, remove from linked list and return success\n2. Check if bHasSize at +0x50 is non-zero - return 0 if invalid\n3. Allocate memory via AllocateMemoryBlockToArray using dwSize at +0x4c\n4. Store allocation header at +0x5c, dereference to get buffer pointer at +0x54\n5. Zero-fill buffer: REP STOSD for dwords (size >> 2), REP STOSB for remaining bytes (size & 3)\n6. Call InitializeResourceAndLock with dwParam2 at +0x58 - return 0 on failure\n7. Call ValidateGameObjectData with dwParam1 at +0x48\n8. Call ReadAndValidateFileData with buffer pointer and size\n9. Call ValidateNonZeroParameter and UpdateTileOffsets for finalization\n10. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n- pTileProject (TileProject*): Structure containing allocation fields at offsets +0x48 to +0x5c\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Success - memory allocated, zeroed, and initialized\n- 0: Failure - size field was zero or initialization failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Re-initialization safe: removes previous allocation from linked list before returning",
