      "name": "ForEach2DArrayElement",
      "signature": "void ForEach2DArrayElement(uint * pConfig, uint * pPixelContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Iterates over a 2D element array and processes each element with ForEachPixelNotEqual.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate configuration flag (bit 0x04) at pConfig[1]\n2. If invalid, assert failure and terminate process\n3. Iterate rows from 0 to row count at pConfig[4]\n4. For each row, iterate columns from 0 to column count at pConfig[5]\n5. Calculate element index: (row * column_count + column)\n6. Call ForEachPixelNotEqual with element pointer, pixel context, and config value\n\nParameters:\n- pConfig (uint*): Configuration structure pointer containing:\n  [0x04] flags (bit 2 = valid configuration flag)\n  [0x0c] processing config value passed to ForEachPixelNotEqual\n  [0x10] row count\n  [0x14] column count  \n  [0x18+] element pointer array (4 bytes per element)\n- pPixelContext (uint*): Context passed to ForEachPixelNotEqual for pixel processing\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value; asserts and terminates on invalid config flag\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x04: Bit mask for valid configuration flag\n- 0x0c: Offset to processing config value\n- 0x10: Offset to row count\n- 0x14: Offset to column count\n- 0x18: Offset to element pointer array start\n- 0x310 (784): Source line number for assert",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:59aa740c8d214c836ff515c46239fa57",
