      "name": "D2CMP_AssertValidFileHandle",
      "signature": "void D2CMP_AssertValidFileHandle(HANDLE hFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Validates file handle and triggers fatal assertion if invalid.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if hFile is zero (invalid handle)\n2. If invalid, call FogAssertFail with \"hFile\" assertion message\n3. Terminate process with exit code -1 via TerminateProcessWithCode\n4. If valid (non-zero), return normally without action\n\nParameters:\n- hFile (HANDLE): File handle to validate, zero indicates error condition\n\nReturns:\n- void: Does not return if handle is invalid (terminates process)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x28a (650): Line number in CelCmp.cpp where assertion occurs\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FogAssertFail (Ordinal_10023): Logs assertion failure\n- TerminateProcessWithCode: Exits process with specified code",
