      "name": "CountAndValidateRunLength",
      "signature": "int CountAndValidateRunLength(byte * pbStart, byte * pbEnd, int nMaxLength, dword * pdwRunComplete, dword * pdwExactMatch)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Count consecutive bytes matching the first byte in range [pbStart, pbEnd).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pbStart < pbEnd, assertion failure if invalid\n2. Load first byte bCurrent = *pbStart\n3. Initialize run length counter nRunLength = 0\n4. Loop through buffer while pbStart < pbEnd:\n   - If current byte != bCurrent OR nRunLength >= nMaxLength, break loop\n   - Increment nRunLength counter\n   - Advance pbStart pointer to next byte\n5. Test if reached end of buffer (pbStart == pbEnd):\n   - If yes (at end): set pdwRunComplete = 1, pdwExactMatch = 0, return nRunLength\n   - If no (stopped early): continue to step 6\n6. For early termination:\n   - Set pdwRunComplete = 0\n   - Scan remaining buffer while pbStart < pbEnd and *pbStart == bCurrent\n   - Set pdwExactMatch = (pbStart == pbEnd) after scanning\n   - Return nRunLength\n\nParameters:\n- pbStart (byte*): Pointer to buffer start (__fastcall ECX)\n- pbEnd (byte*): Pointer to buffer end (__fastcall EDX)\n- nMaxLength (int): Maximum run length before early termination\n- pdwRunComplete (dword*): Output - 1 if run extends to buffer end, 0 if stopped early\n- pdwExactMatch (dword*): Output - 1 if all remaining bytes matched, 0 otherwise\n\nReturns:\n- int: Length of run encountered (0 to nMaxLength), or count at buffer end if pdwRunComplete=1",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9a1f40d78d0e0fedaa9c8d652d141feb",
