      "name": "AppendGameStringToBuffer",
      "signature": "void AppendGameStringToBuffer(char * szDest, int nCheckValue, byte * pbFormatStr, int * pArgList)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Appends game string to destination buffer using conditional source selection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ProcessFormatStringBuffer to preprocess destination and format parameters\n2. Select source string: if nCheckValue==0 or g_pGameStructurePtr is null, use g_pFallbackGamePtr; else use g_pDefaultGamePtr\n3. Scan source string with REPNE SCASB to calculate length (including null terminator)\n4. Scan destination buffer to find end of existing string\n5. Copy source to destination end using DWORD-aligned MOVSD for efficiency\n6. Copy remaining bytes (length & 3) using MOVSB\n\nParameters:\n- szDest (char*): Destination buffer to append string to\n- nCheckValue (int): Source selector flag (0 = use fallback)\n- pbFormatStr (byte*): Format string for preprocessing\n- pArgList (int*): Argument list for format substitutions\n\nReturns:\n- void: Modifies szDest in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses g_pFallbackGamePtr when nCheckValue==0 or g_pGameStructurePtr is null\n- DWORD-aligned copy (SHR 2) optimizes transfer for longer strings",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
